BLOCK FB FB_ShredderSequencerStim
ROOTID 0
NUMBER 9004
LANGUAGE LAD
TITLE "Shredder Sequencer Stimulus Head"
COMMENT "Presents a commanded plant to FB_ShredderSequencer so a conformance index exercises the sequencer against equipment that behaves to order. NETWORKS 1-17 ARE GENERATED - they are the index shell emitted by Harness.Map.StimShellGenerator from this slot's declared spec, and they are mechanism: the index latch and clock, three head and three tail cleardown phases, the scenario, the reset request, the latched-cause check and the four outcomes it publishes, the observation window, completion and re-arm. NETWORKS 18-27 ARE AUTHORED, because each is a claim about the plant rather than mechanism - what the equipment does when the PLC commands it. Phase codes published as Stim.Phase are positional: 1 head disarm, 2 head reset, 3 head verify, 4 scenario, 5 tail disarm, 6 tail reset, 7 tail verify, 0 between indexes; never decode them against another head's. THE FEEDBACK MODEL IS CLOSED-LOOP AND THAT IS NOT A REFINEMENT: the shredder motor block latches a fail-to-run ten seconds after it commands a contactor that does not confirm, and that fault aborts three of the sequencer's step transitions, so a feedback timeline that ignored what the motor was actually commanded would inject aborts no vector asked for. Each modelled contactor answers the output the PLC is really driving, after a delay the vector chooses. THE FAULT RESET IS ARBITRATED, NOT DRIVEN: DB_Controls.FaultReset is one coil shared with the hopper head, the pusher head, the motor block and the pusher block, so the shell publishes a request and Network 19 passes another head's value through whenever this index is not running. Every test-injection member is written the same way, for the same reason. THE STALENESS QUESTION, ANSWERED: the sequencer's dwell timers all key on Step, which this head moves, so every one of them advances; its two staleness-sensitive elements do NOT - ReversalWindowTimer watches for the absence of new reversals and ReversalCount counts entries into Step 60 - and nothing this head can present will move either, because Step 60 is unreachable in the as-built block. That is a property of the block under test, not of this head, and it is recorded here so a green is never read as coverage of them. This head drives the sequencer's inputs and nothing else: it writes the input buffer's own test-injection members, the operator pusher mode, and the operator fault reset."

INTERFACE
  INPUT
  OUTPUT
  STATIC
    Stim : "UDT_ShredderSequencerStim" COMMENT "Caller interface. The harness copy layer writes the command members before an index and reads the published ones while it runs. Member comments live on the type, not repeated here, so the two cannot drift."
      Start : Bool
      ScenarioDone : Bool
      EndAt : Time
      ResetAt : Time
      ResetMode : Int
      ResetRequest : Bool
      ArrivedDirty : Bool
      InertAtStart : Bool
      RecoverFailed : Bool
      InertAtEnd : Bool
      Armed : Bool
      ArmAt : Time
      ArmUntil : Time
      Phase : Int
      PreStartHold : Time
      StartPressWidth : Time
      DischargeConfirmDelay : Time
      RevFeedbackDelay : Time
      FwdFeedbackDelay : Time
      HopperHighAt : Time
      HopperClearAt : Time
      StopAt : Time
      StopByButton : Bool
      StopByDownstreamLoss : Bool
      StopByUnhealthy : Bool
      WithholdDischargeConfirm : Bool
      WithholdRevFeedback : Bool
      WithholdFwdFeedback : Bool
      InjectMotorFault : Bool
    Running : Bool COMMENT "An index is under way: set by Start and held until the index reaches its end, so the harness dropping the start bool part-way through cannot truncate one and produce a short index that still looks complete."
    RunTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    RunT : Time COMMENT "Time since the index started, copied out of the index timer so every phase compares against a plain value."
    ScenT : Time COMMENT "Time since the scenario started, which is the instant the head cleardown finished. Every commanded event time is measured against this and never against the index clock."
    DisarmDwell : Time COMMENT "Length of each disarm phase."
    ResetDwell : Time COMMENT "Length of each reset phase, and therefore the width of the reset pulse inside it."
    VerifyDwell : Time COMMENT "Length of each verify phase - long enough that a latch which was going to re-assert has done so before the outcome is published."
    ResetPulseEnd : Time COMMENT "End of the in-scenario reset pulse under ResetMode 1."
    ResetPulse : Bool COMMENT "A cleardown reset phase is running."
    ScenarioReset : Bool COMMENT "The scenario's own commanded reset is asserted, whichever mode asked for it."
    CauseStanding : Bool COMMENT "Any latched cause the cleardown has to clear is standing right now."
    InHeadDisarm : Bool
    InHeadReset : Bool
    InHeadVerify : Bool
    InScenario : Bool
    InTailDisarm : Bool
    InTailReset : Bool
    InTailVerify : Bool
    HeadDisarmEnd : Time
    HeadResetEnd : Time
    HeadEnd : Time
    ScenarioEnd : Time
    TailDisarmEnd : Time
    TailResetEnd : Time
    TailEnd : Time
    Disarmed : Bool COMMENT "The index is running and the scenario is not - every cleardown phase, head and tail. THIS IS THE DISARM LEVER: while it is true the plant is held stopped at Step 0 and every fault source is held clear, so no cleardown can be defeated by a cause being re-created underneath it."
    StartPressEnd : Time COMMENT "When the commanded cycle-start press ends, so the press window compares against a single time instead of adding one inside a condition."
    StopFired : Bool COMMENT "The scenario has reached its commanded stop instant. WHICH stop it is comes from the three levers, not from this."
    CmdCycleStart : Bool COMMENT "Commanded operator cycle-start button."
    CmdCycleStop : Bool COMMENT "Commanded operator cycle-stop button. Asserted through every cleardown phase as well, which is what holds the plant at Step 0 while the latches are being cleared."
    CmdDownstream : Bool COMMENT "Commanded downstream-running permission. Held true through the cleardown so the only stop reason there is the button, and a cleardown can never be mistaken for a downstream-loss scenario."
    CmdHealthy : Bool COMMENT "Commanded control-circuit healthy input. Held true through the cleardown for the same reason."
    CmdHopperHigh : Bool COMMENT "Commanded hopper high-level sensor."
    CmdMotorFault : Bool COMMENT "Commanded field motor-fault input."
    CmdRunFwdFB : Bool COMMENT "Modelled forward-running feedback - what the contactor is actually reporting back to the PLC."
    CmdRunRevFB : Bool COMMENT "Modelled reverse-running feedback."
    CmdDischargeRunning : Bool COMMENT "Modelled discharge-conveyor running feedback."
    FwdRespTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    RevRespTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
    DischargeRespTimer : TON_TIME VERSION 1.0 SETPOINT
      PT : Time
      ET : Time
      IN : Bool
      Q : Bool
  TEMP
  CONSTANT

NETWORK 1 "Index Latch"
  COIL Running := (Stim.Start OR Running) AND NOT Stim.ScenarioDone

NETWORK 2 "Index Timer"
  TON(RunTimer, IN := Running, PT := T#10M)

NETWORK 3 "Elapsed Index Time"
  MOVE(EN := TRUE, IN := RunTimer.ET) => RunT

NETWORK 4 "Cleardown Dwells"
  MOVE(EN := TRUE, IN := T#15S) => DisarmDwell
  MOVE(EN := TRUE, IN := T#15S) => ResetDwell
  MOVE(EN := TRUE, IN := T#15S) => VerifyDwell

NETWORK 5 "Index Phase Boundaries"
  MOVE(EN := TRUE, IN := DisarmDwell) => HeadDisarmEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := HeadDisarmEnd, IN2 := ResetDwell) => HeadResetEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := HeadResetEnd, IN2 := VerifyDwell) => HeadEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := HeadEnd, IN2 := Stim.EndAt) => ScenarioEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := ScenarioEnd, IN2 := DisarmDwell) => TailDisarmEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := TailDisarmEnd, IN2 := ResetDwell) => TailResetEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := TailResetEnd, IN2 := VerifyDwell) => TailEnd
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := Stim.ResetAt, IN2 := ResetDwell) => ResetPulseEnd

NETWORK 6 "Scenario Elapsed Time"
  MOVE(EN := RunT < HeadEnd, IN := T#0S) => ScenT
  SUB(EN := RunT >= HeadEnd, IN1 := RunT, IN2 := HeadEnd) => ScenT

NETWORK 7 "Index Phases"
  COIL InHeadDisarm := Running AND RunT < HeadDisarmEnd
  COIL InHeadReset := Running AND RunT >= HeadDisarmEnd AND RunT < HeadResetEnd
  COIL InHeadVerify := Running AND RunT >= HeadResetEnd AND RunT < HeadEnd
  COIL InScenario := Running AND RunT >= HeadEnd AND RunT < ScenarioEnd
  COIL InTailDisarm := Running AND RunT >= ScenarioEnd AND RunT < TailDisarmEnd
  COIL InTailReset := Running AND RunT >= TailDisarmEnd AND RunT < TailResetEnd
  COIL InTailVerify := Running AND RunT >= TailResetEnd AND RunT < TailEnd

NETWORK 8 "Reset Windows"
  COIL ResetPulse := InHeadReset OR InTailReset
  COIL ScenarioReset := Stim.ResetMode = 2 OR Stim.ResetMode = 1 AND ScenT >= Stim.ResetAt AND ScenT < ResetPulseEnd

NETWORK 9 "Drive The Fault Reset"
  COIL Stim.ResetRequest := ResetPulse OR InScenario AND ScenarioReset

NETWORK 10 "Latched Cause Standing"
  COIL CauseStanding := iDB_ShredderSequencer.IO.DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault OR iDB_ShredderSequencer.IO.ShredderBlockedFault OR iDB_MotorFwdRevSystem_Shredder.IO.FaultActive

NETWORK 11 "Arrival Inert Check"
  SCOIL Stim.ArrivedDirty := InHeadDisarm AND CauseStanding

NETWORK 12 "Head Cleardown Outcome"
  SCOIL Stim.InertAtStart := InHeadVerify AND NOT CauseStanding
  RCOIL Stim.InertAtStart := InHeadVerify AND CauseStanding

NETWORK 13 "Recovery Outcome"
  SCOIL Stim.RecoverFailed := InTailVerify AND CauseStanding
  SCOIL Stim.InertAtEnd := InTailVerify AND NOT CauseStanding
  RCOIL Stim.InertAtEnd := InTailVerify AND CauseStanding

NETWORK 14 "Observation Window"
  COIL Stim.Armed := InScenario AND ScenT >= Stim.ArmAt AND ScenT < Stim.ArmUntil

NETWORK 15 "Index Complete"
  SCOIL Stim.ScenarioDone := Running AND RunT >= TailEnd

NETWORK 16 "Re-Arm For The Next Index"
  RCOIL Stim.ArrivedDirty := NOT Stim.Start AND NOT Running
  RCOIL Stim.InertAtStart := NOT Stim.Start AND NOT Running
  RCOIL Stim.RecoverFailed := NOT Stim.Start AND NOT Running
  RCOIL Stim.InertAtEnd := NOT Stim.Start AND NOT Running
  RCOIL Stim.ScenarioDone := NOT Stim.Start AND NOT Running

NETWORK 17 "Published Phase"
  MOVE(EN := TRUE, IN := 0) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InHeadDisarm, IN := 1) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InHeadReset, IN := 2) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InHeadVerify, IN := 3) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InScenario, IN := 4) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InTailDisarm, IN := 5) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InTailReset, IN := 6) => Stim.Phase
  MOVE(EN := InTailVerify, IN := 7) => Stim.Phase

NETWORK 18 "Disarm Lever"
  COMMENT "The one bit every cleardown phase depends on. A cleardown assumes nothing can create or re-create a latched cause while it runs, and this block can re-create two of the three: the discharge timeout re-arms whenever Step reaches 20 without a confirm, and the motor's fail-to-run re-arms whenever a contactor is commanded without feedback. Holding this true through all six cleardown phases is what stops the reset pulse landing on a cause that is being re-set underneath it - which would leave no cleardown in the block ever working, in green."
  COIL Disarmed := Running AND NOT InScenario

NETWORK 19 "Arbitrate The Shared Fault Reset"
  COMMENT "DB_Controls.FaultReset is ONE coil and four things want it: this head, the hopper head, the pusher head, and the operator. The generated shell publishes a request rather than driving the line, and this rung is the arbitration: while this index runs the request wins, and at every other moment whatever another head wrote passes through unchanged. Without the pass-through term this head would drive the line low on every scan it is idle, and because the heads run in sequence ahead of the input map, the last one in the sweep would silently disable the reset of every slot before it."
  COIL DB_Controls.FaultReset := Running AND Stim.ResetRequest OR NOT Running AND DB_Controls.FaultReset

NETWORK 20 "Scenario Event Times"
  COMMENT "The two derived instants the drives below compare against, computed once here so no rung adds a duration inside a condition. The stop flag is written above the addition because the readable IR groups statements by kind in one contiguous run and a coil may not follow an arithmetic instruction; neither reads the other, so the order carries no meaning beyond that."
  COIL StopFired := InScenario AND ScenT >= Stim.StopAt
  ADD(EN := TRUE, IN1 := Stim.PreStartHold, IN2 := Stim.StartPressWidth) => StartPressEnd

NETWORK 21 "Commanded Operator Buttons"
  COMMENT "The start press is a window rather than an edge, so it cannot fall between two scans and be missed. The stop button is asserted by the scenario's own lever AND through every cleardown phase, which is how the plant is held at Step 0 while the latches are cleared: it aborts every step to Idle through the sequencer's own stop transitions rather than through anything this head reaches inside the block."
  COIL CmdCycleStart := InScenario AND ScenT >= Stim.PreStartHold AND ScenT < StartPressEnd
  COIL CmdCycleStop := Disarmed OR InScenario AND Stim.StopByButton AND StopFired

NETWORK 22 "Commanded Plant Permissions"
  COMMENT "Downstream running and control-circuit healthy are the other two stop reasons, each on its own lever so a vector names the reason it wants without a code table. Both are held TRUE through the cleardown: the cleardown already stops the plant with the button, and leaving these low as well would make a cleardown indistinguishable from a downstream-loss or unhealthy-circuit scenario. The unhealthy lever reaches the motor block too, so a vector using it is asserting about two blocks. Each negated pair sits at the rail-most position of its AND chain because only the first operand of a chain may be a compound expression - a branch point can occur nowhere else in a series chain."
  COIL CmdDownstream := Disarmed OR NOT (Stim.StopByDownstreamLoss AND StopFired) AND InScenario
  COIL CmdHealthy := Disarmed OR NOT (Stim.StopByUnhealthy AND StopFired) AND InScenario

NETWORK 23 "Commanded Hopper Level And Motor Fault"
  COMMENT "The hopper is high between its two commanded instants and clear outside them; a window at or past the scenario end is how a timeline says it never goes high. The field motor-fault input is the only route by which a vector raises the motor's fault deliberately rather than as a side effect of a withheld feedback, and it is held clear through the cleardown so the motor's own latch can actually be reset."
  COIL CmdHopperHigh := InScenario AND ScenT >= Stim.HopperHighAt AND ScenT < Stim.HopperClearAt
  COIL CmdMotorFault := InScenario AND Stim.InjectMotorFault AND StopFired

NETWORK 24 "Modelled Contactor Response"
  COMMENT "The plant answering the PLC. Each timer starts when the PLC actually drives the output and its Q is the feedback the field would return, so the delay is a contactor pull-in time the vector chooses rather than a fixed instant that happens to line up. Reading the OUTPUT BUFFER rather than the motor block's own coil is deliberate: the buffer is what a field device would be wired to. Drop-out is modelled as instantaneous - a TON resets the moment its input falls - because a lagging drop would present a feedback the PLC is no longer commanding, which is exactly what the motor block latches as a fail-to-stop. Each response is gated on the scenario, so through every cleardown phase all three feedbacks read clear and neither the fail-to-run nor the fail-to-stop detector can re-arm."
  TON(FwdRespTimer, IN := InScenario AND DB_Output.Run_Shredder_Fwd AND NOT Stim.WithholdFwdFeedback, PT := Stim.FwdFeedbackDelay)
  TON(RevRespTimer, IN := InScenario AND DB_Output.Run_Shredder_Rev AND NOT Stim.WithholdRevFeedback, PT := Stim.RevFeedbackDelay)
  TON(DischargeRespTimer, IN := InScenario AND DB_Output.Run_Discharge_Conv AND NOT Stim.WithholdDischargeConfirm, PT := Stim.DischargeConfirmDelay)
  COIL CmdRunFwdFB := FwdRespTimer.Q
  COIL CmdRunRevFB := RevRespTimer.Q
  COIL CmdDischargeRunning := DischargeRespTimer.Q

NETWORK 25 "Force The Monitored Inputs"
  COMMENT "Presents the commanded plant to the input map through the input buffer's own test-injection members, which is the facility the map already provides: with the flag set the map ignores the physical terminal and takes each input from its test member. EVERY RUNG PASSES THROUGH WHEN THIS INDEX IS NOT RUNNING, and that is not defensive style - it is required. Test[] is one array shared by every stimulus head in the program, all of them run ahead of the input map, and a plain coil would drive another slot's commanded input low on every scan this one is idle; whichever head ran last in the sweep would win and the others would be silently disarmed. Test[0] is the map's own injection enable and is shared the same way. Outside an index every one of these passes through and the map reads the field."
  COIL DB_Input.Test[0] := Running OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[0]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[1] := Running AND CmdHealthy OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[1]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[3] := Running AND CmdCycleStart OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[3]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[4] := Running AND CmdCycleStop OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[4]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[5] := Running AND CmdRunFwdFB OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[5]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[6] := Running AND CmdRunRevFB OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[6]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[7] := Running AND CmdMotorFault OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[7]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[8] := Running AND CmdHopperHigh OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[8]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[10] := Running AND CmdDischargeRunning OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[10]
  COIL DB_Input.Test[15] := Running AND CmdDownstream OR NOT Running AND DB_Input.Test[15]

NETWORK 26 "Hold The Pusher Parked"
  COMMENT "The sequencer's PreStartSounder output is its own step-10 siren OR the pusher's jog warning, and its PusherModeCmd passes the operator mode straight through whenever no hard stop is forcing mode 0. Holding the operator mode at 0 for the whole index is what keeps the pusher parked and jog-blocked, so the siren this slot observes is the sequencer's and not the pusher's. IT IS A DECLARED PLANT ASSUMPTION, NOT A DERIVATION: nothing here proves the pusher stays quiet, and if the pusher slot ever runs concurrently with this one the assumption fails - which is why PreStartSounder's resting value is declared excluded in this slot's binding rather than given a number."
  MOVE(EN := Running, IN := 0) => DB_Controls.PusherMode

